  "Question": "Find \\(\\sin 30^\\circ\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "1/2",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(\\sin 30^\\circ=1/2\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Use a right-triangle side ratio\n\nA right triangle with a \\(30^\\circ\\) angle gives a geometric way to find the sine. Let its hypotenuse have length \\(h>0\\). The side opposite \\(30^\\circ\\) has length \\(h/2\\), so the definition of sine gives\n\\[\n\\sin30^\\circ=\\frac{h/2}{h}=\\frac12.\n\\]",
